NNAAMMEE
       ttooee - list table of entries of _t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o terminal types

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ttooee [--aahhss] [--vv [_n]] [_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y ...]

       ttooee [--uu|--UU] _f_i_l_e

       ttooee --VV

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ttooee  reports  to the standard output stream the (primary) names and de‐
       scriptions of the terminal types available  to  the  _t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o  library.
       Each  _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y  is  scanned;  if none are given, ttooee scans the default
       _t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o directory.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       The --hh option can be helpful to observe where ttooee is looking for termi‐
       nal descriptions.  Other options support maintainers of _t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o termi‐
       nal descriptions.

       --aa       lists entries from all terminal database directories that _t_e_r_‐
                _m_i_n_f_o would search, instead of only the first that it finds.

                If   --ss   is   also  given,  ttooee  additionally  reports,  like
                _c_o_n_f_l_i_c_t(1), which entries  correspond  to  a  given  terminal
                database.   An  “*”  marks  entries that differ, and “+” marks
                equivalent entries.

                Without the --ss option, ttooee does not attempt  to  merge  dupli‐
                cates in its report.

       --hh       writes a heading naming each each directory as it is accessed.

       --ss       sorts the output by the entry names.

       --uu _f_i_l_e  lists  terminal  type  dependencies  in _f_i_l_e, a _t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o entry
                source or _t_e_r_m_c_a_p database file.  The  report  summarizes  the
                “uussee”  (_t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o)  and  ttcc (_t_e_r_m_c_a_p) relations: each line com‐
                prises the primary name of a terminal  type  employing  uussee/ttcc
                capabilities, a colon, a space- and tab-separated list of pri‐
                mary names of terminal types thus named, and a newline.

       --UU _f_i_l_e  lists terminal type reverse dependencies in _f_i_l_e,  a  _t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o
                entry  source or _t_e_r_m_c_a_p database file.  The report summarizes
                the “uussee” (_t_e_r_m_i_n_f_o) and ttcc (_t_e_r_m_c_a_p) reverse relations:  each
                line  comprises  the primary name of a terminal type occurring
                in uussee/ttcc capabilities, a colon, a  space-  and  tab-separated
                list  of primary names of terminal types naming them thus, and
                a newline.

       --vv [_n]   reports verbose  status  information  to  the  standard  error
                stream, showing ttooee's progress.

                The optional parameter _n is an integer between 1 and 10 inclu‐
                sive, interpreted as for ttiicc(1M).  If _n_c_u_r_s_e_s is built without
                tracing support, _n is ignored.

       --VV       reports  the  version  of _n_c_u_r_s_e_s associated with this program
                and exits with a successful status.

